3d6d089f0ba8daf\",\n      \"plan.md\": \"2ac87d1a99d6b98c0569771c168d7067c5ee62f21c1a02b5aa84370215983177\",\n      \"tasks.md\": \"014387cdd264b47dfaa874f44d2b05c7cf0e480bfd7bb66ca044f79b5730d0ad\",\n      \"implementation-summary.md\": \"2c7eafade818a899b1b22b028d37688a90320d5f9cf4d505674783960b1d639a\"\n    },\n    \"last_active_at\": null\n  }\n}\n--- task count / REQ check ---\n92:| REQ-001 | With `--min-percent <N>`, a spec-folder run whose Overall Completion is below N exits 3 | `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 90 /tmp/minpct-demo` exits 3 on the 77% fixture |\n93:| REQ-002 | With `--min-percent <N>`, a spec-folder run whose Overall Completion is at or above N exits 0 | `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 70 /tmp/minpct-demo` exits 0, and `--min-percent 77` also exits 0 |\n99:| REQ-003 | The printed report is byte-identical with and without `--min-percent` | `diff` of the two runs prints nothing for both the text and the `--json` report |\n100:| REQ-004 | `--help` documents the option and its exit status | `calculate-completeness.sh --help \\| rg -c -- '--min-percent'` prints 2 |\n101:| REQ-005 | A missing, empty or non-integer N exits 1 with an error on stderr | `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent /tmp/minpct-demo` exits 1, and `--min-percent abc /tmp/minpct-demo` exits 1 |\n102:| REQ-006 | `--min-percent` combined with `--file` exits 1, because no Overall Completion exists to compare | `calculate-completeness.sh --min-percent 90 --file specs/x/spec.md` exits 1 with an error naming the conflict |\n103:| REQ-007 | When `--json` and `--min-percent <N>` are passed together, the JSON output gains a boolean field `min_percent_met`, true when Overall Completion is at or above N and false otherwise | `calculate-completeness.sh --json --min-percent 90 /tmp/minpct-demo \\| rg -c '\"min_percent_met\": false'` prints 1, and the same run with `--min-percent 70` prints 1 for `\"min_percent_met\": true` |\n124:| Risk | Exit 3 is the spec-script taxonomy's system-error code, so a caller may read a below-threshold result as a crash | A caller retries or aborts on what is a normal gate result | Document exit 3 in `show_help` and in the script's trailing exit-code comment, and name it in REQ-004 |\n50:- [ ] T014 Add the `min_percent_met` boolean to the `--json` report when `MIN_PERCENT` is set, true at or above the threshold and false below it (REQ-007) (`$C`). Verify: `bash $C --json --min-percent 90 /tmp/minpct-demo | rg -c '\"min_percent_met\": false'` prints 1.\n"}}],"_meta":{"cognition.ai/cwd":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-michelkerkmeester-MEGA-Development-Code-Environment-Public/fcd93cd7-b3f2-45e6-b976-87fabe792df3/scratchpad/speed-loop/w776a5f2639/tree","terminal_exit":{"terminal_id":"5ad9d6","exit_code":0,"signal":null},"cognition.ai/inferenceToolName":"exec"}}
